<title>USA: TABLE-First Chicago NBD Corp Q2 net.</title>
<headline>TABLE-First Chicago NBD Corp Q2 net.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr primary		$1.20		    $1.10</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$1.20		    $1.09</p>
<p> Net			378,000		  361,000</p>
<p> Net int. income	951,000		  935,000</p>
<p> Nonint. income	 644,000		  643,000</p>
<p> Loan loss prov	 180,000		  185,000</p>
<p> Avg total assets     108,292		  116,280</p>
<p> Return on equity	  18.1		     17.4</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     310,900		  320,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     311,300		  326,900</p>
<p>6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$2.38		    $2.14</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$2.37		    $2.12</p>
<p> Net			758,000		  701,000</p>
<p> Net int. income    1,858,000		1,848,000</p>
<p> Nonint. income     1,323,000		1,269,000</p>
<p> Loan loss prov	 367,000		  360,000</p>
<p> Avg total assets     106,721		  118,494</p>
<p> Return on equity	  17.9		     17.0</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     313,700		  319,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     316,200		  326,400</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers. Return in equity is in percent.)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q2 credit card chargeoff rate was 7.7 percent, compared to 7.4 percent in Q1 and 5.9 percent a year ago.</p>
<p>Q2 trading revenues were $36 million, up from $22 million a year ago.</p>
<p>Q2 market-driven revenues, which include trading profits, equity securities gains and investment securities gains were $86 million, down from $110 million a year ago.</p>
<p>Assets at June 30 were $112.60 billiion, compared to $113.71 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
